  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "The Holocaust History Museum preserves its triangular concrete spine, photographed side entrance, west overlook and flared wings, two mapped access bridges and the circular Hall of Names roof light. The glass ridge clears the buried central stretch and breaks at the native road and footpath. The model covers the exterior and controls the transition to the standard terrain.",
    "identityBasis": "Distinct OSM way 74078313 and native building 35184446167145 identify the museum within the shared Q156591 campus. The east gable, west flared wings and two mapped bridge ends fix the signed frame. The long axis is built in east/south coordinates and uses heading zero. The Hall of Names belongs to the museum. The Hall of Remembrance and other campus ranges have separate placements.",
    "heightBasis": "Working interior floor 794.2 m. The standard terrain supplies the central ridge profile and covering elevations at the two mapped crossings. Both terminal profiles and the Hall of Names roof use the ordinary aerial and exterior photographs.",
    "terrainBasis": "The off-footprint Terrarium sample fixes the datum. The buried gallery range retains native terrain over both sides. Two bridge portions follow the PMTiles footway endpoints and join the native approaches. The west stairs and terminal heights are picture-led approximations.",
